Has anyone been able to get NetHack to run inside GNU Emacs?  I guess one would
fire up a shell and run it from there.. I've tried this but the TERMCAP setting
is no good; I get the message "OOPSTerminal must backspace."  Does anyone have
any ideas?

My reason for wanting to run NetHack inside Emacs is to possibly take advantage
of Emacs' macro capability, even to creating a nethack-mode for Emacs!
Something along these lines came up in an article a couple of days ago, where
someone suggested making NetHack the "Emacs of games".  Why bother when you can
create a nethack-mode.el and run NetHack in Emacs and get the advantages of
Emacs' macro capabilities.  Imagine: M-x nethack-kill-wizard etc...

